{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>I have surely remembered you.</b> Two visitations: one for Israel, and the second for the Shekhinah, which descended with Jacob our father, peace be upon him, to Egypt — for it was with them in their affliction. This is the letter ה (heh) alluded to in the verse (Genesis 46:4): ״אנכי ארד עמך מצרימה ואנכי אעלך גם עלה״ — as I have written there. And it is Kenesset Yisrael, which Scripture calls ״צעקת בני ישראל״. And this is what it says: אתכם — 'you' — ואת העשוי לכם — 'and that which was done to you' — in Egypt; that is, you and the letter ה (heh), which is in affliction with you in Egypt. And the expression עשוי is from the language of (Zephaniah 3:19): ״הנני עושה את כל מעניך״ — that is, I suffer pain over your affliction. And understand this." "<b>Furthermore,</b> it may be interpreted as two visitations: one in the attribute of mercy upon Israel, and from this the verse says ״פקדתי אתכם״; and the second in the attribute of judgment upon the Egyptians, for what they did to them in Egypt, and from this it says ״ואת העשוי לכם במצרים״. For thus He promised Abraham (Genesis 15:14): ״וגם את הגוי אשר יעבדו דן אנכי״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:54.123276433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}